          "text": "🇵🇱 Poland has officially banned the Communist Party\n\nPoland’s Constitutional Tribunal has ruled to ban the Communist Party of the Republic of Poland, stating that its program and ideology violate the Constitution. \n\nThe court emphasized that there is “no place in the Polish legal system for a party that glorifies the crimes of communism.”\n\nThe ruling effectively dissolves the party, which has existed since 2002.\n\nThe liquidation process has been ongoing for several years: the issue was first raised by the Prosecutor General back in 2020. \n\nIn November of this year, Polish President Karol Nawrocki once again submitted a motion to the Constitutional Tribunal.\n\nDespite its marginal status, the Communist Party of Poland had, according to various estimates, from several hundred to around a thousand members."
